usage: gitreins [-h] [--version]
                {install,push-check,quality-ensure,init,setup,disable,enable,uninstall,config-validate,doctor,fingerprint,task,review,worktree,guard,judge,commit,commit-audit,resolve,preflight,mcp-server,security-scan,setup-tools,qa,report,serve} ...

GitReins — Git-Native Agent Co-Harness

positional arguments:
  {install,push-check,quality-ensure,init,setup,disable,enable,uninstall,config-validate,doctor,fingerprint,task,review,worktree,guard,judge,commit,commit-audit,resolve,preflight,mcp-server,security-scan,setup-tools,qa,report,serve}
    install             Install GitReins hooks and config in the current repo
    push-check          Scan outgoing commit content for secrets
    quality-ensure      Run the repo's quality producer to completion and
                        enforce block-mode (pre-push)
    init                Smart init — detect language, size, optimal config
    setup               Guided setup: smart config, hooks, then a health check
                        that decides done
    disable             Disarm the hooks without removing config or history
    enable              Re-arm the hooks after `gitreins disable`
    uninstall           Remove the hooks and config GitReins installed (dry-
                        run by default)
    config-validate     Check .gitreins/config.yaml for unknown keys, wrong
                        types and bad values
    doctor              Validate .gitleaks.toml (and migrate pre-DF-001 glob
                        allowlist entries)
    fingerprint         Hash the final Git-visible workspace content without
                        mutating the repo
    task                Task management
    review              Manage persistent review findings
    worktree            Git worktree diagnostics and task worktree lifecycle
    guard               Run Tier 1 guards
    judge               Evaluate a task
    commit              Commit with guard checks
    commit-audit        Validate commit message against staged diff (commit-
                        msg hook)
    resolve             Resolve a question against the repo's code (Jev
                        resolution gate)
    preflight           Pre-dispatch premise check: resolve a row, get a
                        dispatch decision
    mcp-server          Run MCP stdio server
    security-scan       Run the Antares CVE localization scanner (opt-in)
    setup-tools         Show available static analysis tools and install
                        instructions
    qa                  QA run ledger — record and read QA run outcomes
    report              Show verdict history
    serve               Live judgment browser — local web server (Ctrl-C to
                        stop)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
